# The scenario editor's commands that edit-1939 does not play, written by hand. On the 1939
# scenario, Allied side:
#   - Army at Paris: Edit, the strength one step up and the type changed to Infantry; Place, a new
#     army of the first type and nation, with a 50% chance of appearing; Rotate, the first army
#     of the stack to the top; Remove, Yes, which removes Infantry 5;
#   - Army at Berlin, which holds an Axis army: the editor asks to remove it first (Yes), then
#     places an Allied army there (in slot 5, the first one free), of the first type and nation,
#     always;
#   - Navy, Move: to Cherbourg, the only city whose name starts with C;
#   - Air Force (by the arrows, since A is Army): Move to Reims, then Edit, one plane more;
#   - Cities: the first city, Amsterdam, given to the Axis side;
#   - Capital (by the arrows, since C is Cities): Reims.
# It then saves the scenario as 1939, loads it back, saves it again and quits. The run's saved
# files are checked by their hashes. The save holds the two cases that the original Save got wrong
# (docs/devnotes.md, item 18): an Axis slot emptied in the middle (Berlin's army, slot 32), and an
# Allied army with a 50% chance, whose location is negative. All six Allied and three Axis armies
# must be saved. The second Save first copies the first one to ww1939.bak and euro1939.bak, so
# each .bak must have the same hash as the file saved after it: the load lost nothing, not even
# the 50% chance, which the editor's loader once dropped.
# Each city menu takes the first letter of a city, Up and Down for the city before or after, and
# Enter.
#! program edit
#! files scenarios/WW1939.INI scenarios/WW1939.BAK scenarios/EURO1939.DAT scenarios/EURO1939.BAK

# Starting Year: EURO1939.DAT.
play until 2:S
key enter

# Army, Paris (by its letter): the menu of the city's army.
play until 2:M
digest
text a
play until 2:C
text p
play until 2:C
digest
key enter
# Edit: Strength, one step up; Type, Infantry; then Esc.
play until 2:P
digest
text e
play until 2:U
text s
play until 7
key up
play until 7
digest
key enter
play until 2:U
text t
play until 2:C
digest
key enter
play until 2:U
digest
key esc

# Army, Paris (where the city menu now starts): Place, the first type and nation, and 50%.
play until 2:M
text a
play until 2:C
key enter
play until 2:P
text p
play until 2:U
digest
key enter
play until 2:N
digest
key enter
play until 2:C
digest
text 5

# Army, Paris: Rotate, the first army of the stack (Infantry 5) to the top.
play until 2:M
digest
text a
play until 2:C
key enter
play until 2:P
text r
play until 2
digest
key enter

# Army, Paris: Remove (the last entry), Yes. It removes Infantry 5, so slot 5 is empty and the army
# with a 50% chance stays, in slot 6.
play until 2:M
digest
text a
play until 2:C
key enter
play until 2:P
key pagedown
prompt
key enter
play until 2:R
digest
text y

# Army, Berlin (B is Belgrade, then Down): remove the Axis army, Yes; then place an Allied army.
play until 2:M
digest
text a
play until 2:C
text b
play until 2:C
key down
play until 2:C
digest
key enter
play until 2:R
digest
text y
play until 2:U
digest
key enter
play until 2:N
key enter
play until 2:C
key enter

# Navy, Move: Cherbourg.
play until 2:M
digest
text n
play until 2:N
text m
play until 2:C
text c
play until 2:C
digest
key enter

# Air Force, the fourth entry (PgUp, then Down three times): Move, Reims.
play until 2:M
digest
key pageup
prompt
key down
prompt
key down
prompt
key down
prompt
key enter
play until 2:A
digest
text m
play until 2:C
text r
play until 2:C
digest
key enter
# Air Force again: Edit, one plane more.
play until 2:M
digest
key pageup
prompt
key down
prompt
key down
prompt
key down
prompt
key enter
play until 2:A
text e
play until 7
digest
key up
play until 7
key enter

# Cities: Amsterdam, the first city; the Axis side, the second entry.
play until 2:M
digest
text c
play until 2:C
digest
key enter
play until 2:O
digest
key down
prompt
key enter

# Capital, the eighth entry (PgUp, then Down seven times): Reims, the first city whose name starts
# with R.
play until 2:M
digest
key pageup
prompt
key down
prompt
key down
prompt
key down
prompt
key down
prompt
key down
prompt
key down
prompt
key down
prompt
key enter
play until 2:C
text r
play until 2:C
digest
key enter

# Save, the fourth entry from the end: as 1939, its month as it is, its description as it is.
play until 2:M
digest
key pagedown
prompt
key up
prompt
key up
prompt
key up
prompt
key enter
play until 2:S
key enter
play until 2:B
key enter
play until 4
key enter

# Load: 1939 again, now the saved scenario, with every army in its place.
play until 2:M
digest
text l
play until 2:S
key enter

# Save again, as before: the first save becomes the .bak files.
play until 2:M
digest
key pagedown
prompt
key up
prompt
key up
prompt
key up
prompt
key enter
play until 2:S
key enter
play until 2:B
key enter
play until 4
key enter

# Quit, then Yes by its letter, and a key for END's "Press any key to continue".
play until 2:M
digest
text q
play until 2:L
text y
repeat space
